### Data-driven convergence: change one Hiera value ###

The manifest is not edited at all here. Only puppet/data/common.yaml
changes -- the examination-eligibility threshold, 75 -> 80. A convergence
tool should therefore change exactly the resources that depend on that
value, and nothing else.

--- before ---
ATTENDANCE_ELIGIBILITY_THRESHOLD=75
{"app":{"name":"Student Attendance Management Portal","environment":"production"}}

--- changing the Hiera value ---
  attendance::app_eligibility_threshold: 80

--- puppet apply ---
Notice: Compiled catalog for a2ed425e20bf in environment production in 0.40 seconds
Notice: /Stage[main]/Attendance::Config/File[/etc/attendance/attendance.env]/content: content changed '{sha256}7810418268a72b91ae91469a3448b4d966ef4dd731c5cc5b215a3ab4bc67db60' to '{sha256}fdb2b1cf753b3d7b7ad5c3e52eb47b79cc9cd4859c099d261ed694f19b20603e'
Notice: /Stage[main]/Attendance::Service/Service[attendance]: Triggered 'refresh' from 1 event
Notice: Applied catalog in 2.84 seconds
detailed-exitcode=2

--- after ---
ATTENDANCE_ELIGIBILITY_THRESHOLD=80
{"status":"UP"}

--- reverting the Hiera value to 75 and re-applying ---
Notice: Compiled catalog for a2ed425e20bf in environment production in 0.40 seconds
Notice: /Stage[main]/Attendance::Config/File[/etc/attendance/attendance.env]/content: content changed '{sha256}fdb2b1cf753b3d7b7ad5c3e52eb47b79cc9cd4859c099d261ed694f19b20603e' to '{sha256}7810418268a72b91ae91469a3448b4d966ef4dd731c5cc5b215a3ab4bc67db60'
Notice: /Stage[main]/Attendance::Service/Service[attendance]: Triggered 'refresh' from 1 event
Notice: Applied catalog in 3.29 seconds
detailed-exitcode=2

ATTENDANCE_ELIGIBILITY_THRESHOLD=75
health: {"status":"UP"}

The value is data, not code: the same manifest produces either state
depending only on puppet/data/common.yaml, and converges back again.
